#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:0
msgid ""
"Unlock and access the data on a disk protected by hardware-backed encryption "
"using your recovery key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:7
msgid "Topics: Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:11
msgid "Recover data from hardware-backed disk encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:13
msgid ""
"If you know your {ref}`recovery key <tpm-fde-recovery-key>`, you can access "
"the data on your disk secured with {ref}`hardware-backed disk encryption "
"<hardware-backed-disk-encryption>` (TPM/FDE) even from a different system. "
"For example, you can unlock the disk while a live Linux session is running "
"on your computer, or after you've connected the disk to another computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:16
msgid "What you'll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:18
msgid "You must know the recovery key to your disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:19
msgid ""
"You must access the disk using a Linux system that can install snaps, such "
"as using Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:20
msgid "The disk must not be corrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:23
msgid "Unlock the disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:25
msgid ""
"Check if the `snap` command is available on your system. If not, [install it]"
"(https://snapcraft.io/docs/tutorials/install-the-daemon/#tutorials-install-"
"the-daemon-index)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:27
msgid ""
"Install the `snap-tpmctl` tool. You can either use the App Center or the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:37
msgid ""
"Examine the partitions on your encrypted disk. On Ubuntu Desktop, you can "
"use the Disks application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:39
msgid ""
"Note down the device path of the partition that you want to recover, such as "
"`/dev/nvme0n1p4`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:41
msgid "Mount the encrypted partition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:51
msgid ""
"Replace `/dev/nvme0n1p4` with your device path. Replace `/mnt` with the "
"directory where you want to mount the partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:53
msgid "Enter your recovery key when prompted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/recover-data-from-hardware-backed-disk-encryption.md:55
msgid ""
"In your file browser, open the mount point (such as `/mnt`) to access the "
"data on the encrypted partition."
msgstr ""

